<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest of Tura Notes for iOS (required by Apple since 05/2024).

  Written from the RELEASE binary, not from the debug one: the device archive
  (`tauri ios build --target aarch64 --no-sign --archive-only`) was scanned with
  `nm -u` and `otool -s __TEXT __objc_methname` on 12/10/2026, and this file
  declares exactly the required-reason categories that scan found. A debug
  build is not evidence: it keeps every unused objc2 binding (`systemUptime`,
  `NSUserDefaults`) that the release link strips.

  - NSPrivacyTracking is false and no tracking domain exists: there is no
    analytics, advertising or telemetry SDK in the binary (docs/SCOPE.md, section 13).
  - NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty. The app collects nothing for itself.
    Notes stay on the device; what leaves it goes to a server or an AI provider
    that the USER configures, with the user's own credential. Whether that counts
    as "collected" in the App Store Connect privacy questionnaire is the owner's
    decision, answered there and not in this file.
  - FileTimestamp, C617.1: stat, fstat, lstat and fstatat are imported, and the
    app reads the modification time of notes to detect an outside change
    (notes-fs, notes-core). Today every workspace is inside the app container
    (Documents). When the security-scoped-bookmark adapter lands, files outside
    it are read too, and 3B52.1 (files the user granted access to) must be added.
  - DiskSpace, E174.1: statfs and fstatfs are imported by the bundled SQLite
    (it asks the filesystem which locking it can use), and the app's writes
    refuse cleanly on a full disk (tools/enospc.sh).
  - Not declared, on purpose: UserDefaults, SystemBootTime (mach_absolute_time
    and systemUptime are not imported; clock_gettime is not on Apple's list),
    ActiveKeyboards. If App Store Connect answers the first upload with
    ITMS-91053 for any of them, add the block and say so in the changelog.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
      <dict>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
        <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
        <array>
          <string>C617.1</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
      <dict>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
        <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
        <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
        <array>
          <string>E174.1</string>
        </array>
      </dict>
    </array>
  </dict>
</plist>
